{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792401058,"nonce":"XDd6zEMrGI2uXx7jIxvBeRkAT70=","title":"Theme Studio and custom fonts for theme bundles","message":"`rayde name.raytheme` opens the file as a project: the Theme Studio page (identity, colours per scheme, typography and font files, shape and spacing, stylesheets, component preview), the window wearing the theme as the text is edited, problems on their lines, Install.\n\nTheme bundles gain a `fonts` section: font files beside the theme (.ttf, .otf, .ttc, .woff2) grouped by family, registered with ashui.text.Fonts when the theme is in force, copied on install, family checked against the TrueType/OpenType name table.\n\nAlso in this change: Theming loads and removes a theme's sheets with Css.load/remove (no accumulation), ThemeFile reads from text and locates problems by path, ThemeEdit edits values in place, `.raytheme`/`.rayext` highlight as JSON, packaging registers .raytheme.\n\nKnown limit: changing `typography.sans` while RayDE runs does not repaint text nodes that already exist; new nodes take the font. Reported to ashui (ashui-8c). Repro: `SNAPSHOT_ONLY=themestudio scripts/snapshot.sh`, step `fonts-sans`.","files":null}]}